<TrustPage
  title="Contact Havemoon"
  description="Contact Havemoon about editorial corrections, source questions, privacy requests, technical problems, or sourcing services."
  updated="August 12, 2026"
>
  <h2>Email</h2>
  <p>
    Write to <a href="mailto:contact@havemoon.com">contact@havemoon.com</a>. This address is used
    for editorial questions, correction reports, privacy requests, accessibility or technical
    problems, and clearly identified business inquiries.
  </p>

  <h2>Other official channels</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Company and sourcing-service information:
      <a href="https://havemoon.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">havemoon.com</a>
    </li>
    <li>
      Reproducible website defects and broken links:
      <a
        href="https://github.com/awalm2875/havemoon-knowledge-ScoringSOHO/issues"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">public issue tracker</a
      >
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p class="trust-note">
    GitHub issues are public. Do not post personal data, supplier bank information, identity
    documents, confidential quotations, product files, or other sensitive material there. Use email
    for privacy requests or matters that should not be public.
  </p>

  <h2>What to include</h2>
  <p>
    For a content question, include the page URL, relevant heading, and source or evidence. Do not
    send supplier bank details, identity documents, product secrets, personal data, or other
    confidential files through a general contact channel.
  </p>

  <h2>Editorial boundaries</h2>
  <p>
    Havemoon cannot confirm product compliance, customs classification, legal status, supplier
    legitimacy, or shipment instructions from a short message. Those decisions require
    transaction-specific evidence and appropriately qualified professionals.
  </p>
</TrustPage>
